00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:40.670
API in our data
discovery tools, we

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:43.010
would like to introduce
GOJEK to you first.

00:23:43.010 --> 00:23:46.220
So GOJEK is actually
a technology company

00:23:46.220 --> 00:23:50.840
that have purpose to improve
people's quality of life, OK?

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:54.040
And so I believe not many
of you know that, actually,

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:57.470
GOJEK starting as a
call center in 2010

00:23:57.470 --> 00:24:00.200
for the ojek services,
which is-- ojek,

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:03.230
actually, is a term in
Indonesia for motorcycle ride

00:24:03.230 --> 00:24:05.550
hailing or a motorcycle taxi.

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:10.400
Five years after that,
we launch our mobile apps

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:14.150
with three initial services,
which is GO-RIDE, GO-SEND,

00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:15.440
and GO-SHOP.

00:24:15.440 --> 00:24:18.260
And starting in
2016, we would like

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:20.600
to become a mobile
app for daily needs.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:24.140
And we are starting to expand
into more than 200 province

00:24:24.140 --> 00:24:28.130
in Indonesia and launch
more than 20 services.

00:24:28.130 --> 00:24:31.880
And just last year, 2018,
we are making history

00:24:31.880 --> 00:24:35.670
by doing international
expansion to Vietnam, Thailand,

00:24:35.670 --> 00:24:38.840
and Singapore.

00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:42.020
In the beginning, GOJEK is
built to provide a solution

00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:44.000
for our informal sectors.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:46.550
Because here in Indonesia,
we have so many challenge

00:24:46.550 --> 00:24:48.350
for the informal sector.

00:24:48.350 --> 00:24:51.000
Some of the challenge that
tools like GOJEK solve is,

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:54.890
first, we would like
to solve inefficiency

00:24:54.890 --> 00:24:58.400
of time and accessibility, both
for the customer and service

00:24:58.400 --> 00:24:59.660
provider.

00:24:59.660 --> 00:25:01.490
Because in early
days, if you would

00:25:01.490 --> 00:25:05.480
like to have ojek services, we
need to go to the Main Street.

00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:08.510
We need to find an
available object there.

00:25:08.510 --> 00:25:11.450
And in the other hand, most
of the time from the service

00:25:11.450 --> 00:25:14.640
provider itself are wasting
to waiting for the customer

00:25:14.640 --> 00:25:17.190
rather than providing
the service.

00:25:17.190 --> 00:25:19.580
And the last one,
GOJEK would like also

00:25:19.580 --> 00:25:23.070
to empower our service provider
for the financial services

00:25:23.070 --> 00:25:26.510
so they are able to plan their
future and sort of only earning

00:25:26.510 --> 00:25:29.810
money for one day.

00:25:29.810 --> 00:25:31.140
RENATA KUMALA: So hi, everyone.

00:25:31.140 --> 00:25:32.270
My name is Renata.

00:25:32.270 --> 00:25:34.580
And I'm currently
the product manager

00:25:34.580 --> 00:25:38.090
in the business intelligence
core team at GOJEK.

00:25:38.090 --> 00:25:43.280
So like just what
Dimas say, we--

00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:47.600
at GOJEK, we are here
to solve real problems.

00:25:47.600 --> 00:25:52.880
And when we started
off in 2010, we

00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:55.850
started off with just one
service, which is just a ride

00:25:55.850 --> 00:25:57.390
hailing business.

00:25:57.390 --> 00:25:59.420
However, as time--
as you can imagine,

00:25:59.420 --> 00:26:01.520
in Indonesia, we
are a developing

00:26:01.520 --> 00:26:04.370
as well as a growing nation.

00:26:04.370 --> 00:26:06.200
So there are a lot
of problems that

00:26:06.200 --> 00:26:08.300
are there to be solved,
a lot of opportunity

00:26:08.300 --> 00:26:09.800
that we can help on.

00:26:09.800 --> 00:26:12.770
And that's the reason
why we grow to,

00:26:12.770 --> 00:26:18.170
now, more than 20
services in 2018.

00:26:18.170 --> 00:26:22.940
So when you hear more
than 20 services,

00:26:22.940 --> 00:26:25.280
like, what can you
provide to your user?

00:26:25.280 --> 00:26:27.590
There seems to be
too many services.

00:26:27.590 --> 00:26:31.340
So we provide the user
ranging from payment services,

00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:38.150
to financial services, as
well as lifestyle services

00:26:38.150 --> 00:26:39.080
like GO-GLAM.

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:43.820
So GO-GLAM is basically,
you can get connected

00:26:43.820 --> 00:26:46.550
to a professional hairstylist.

00:26:46.550 --> 00:26:49.340
And that hairstylist
can come to your home

00:26:49.340 --> 00:26:51.950
and get you a fresh new look.

00:26:51.950 --> 00:26:55.940
Or we have GO-DAILY, which is
basically a daily subscription

00:26:55.940 --> 00:26:56.850
service.

00:26:56.850 --> 00:27:01.550
So you can get delivered
your daily household needs

00:27:01.550 --> 00:27:05.960
like tissues, rice, mineral
water on a scheduled basis.

00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:09.450
Either you want it on a weekly
basis or a monthly basis.

00:27:09.450 --> 00:27:11.990
So we're not only
growing in terms

00:27:11.990 --> 00:27:14.930
of the number of services that
we are providing to our user,

00:27:14.930 --> 00:27:16.580
but also regionally.

00:27:16.580 --> 00:27:18.890
So we are now live
not only, obviously,

00:27:18.890 --> 00:27:22.110
in Indonesia, but also
in Singapore, Thailand,

00:27:22.110 --> 00:27:23.520
and Vietnam.

00:27:23.520 --> 00:27:26.030
And user have
interesting at by--

00:27:26.030 --> 00:27:30.410
you can see the numbers, with
130 million apps download.

00:27:30.410 --> 00:27:33.500
We are partnering with
more than 2 million drivers

00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:37.110
and 400,000 more merchants.

00:27:37.110 --> 00:27:40.280
And we are now
transacting more than 100

00:27:40.280 --> 00:27:42.760
million monthly transactions.

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:49.510
So as our business
grow, so does our data.

00:27:49.510 --> 00:27:52.290
As you can imagine, when
you add one service tag,

00:27:52.290 --> 00:27:54.240
and/or you add--

00:27:54.240 --> 00:27:57.730
you expand to one more region,
it doesn't goes linearly.

00:27:57.730 --> 00:28:00.030
It just doesn't go, like,
when you want services,

00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:00.970
you add one database.

00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:02.420
It doesn't go like that.

00:28:02.420 --> 00:28:06.180
So the data costs have
become much more complex.

00:28:06.180 --> 00:28:09.030
Even though we
are using BigQuery

00:28:09.030 --> 00:28:11.370
as our data warehouse,
which already simplify

00:28:11.370 --> 00:28:14.340
a lot of these
complexities, however, data

00:28:14.340 --> 00:28:16.020
is not just raw
data that you get

00:28:16.020 --> 00:28:17.940
from your application, right?

00:28:17.940 --> 00:28:19.650
It also include
dashboard that you

00:28:19.650 --> 00:28:22.890
have, and a lot of
data visualization tool

00:28:22.890 --> 00:28:26.060
like Metabase, Tableau,
and also analyses

00:28:26.060 --> 00:28:28.370
that a lot of your data
teams have created.

00:28:28.370 --> 00:28:30.930
Like, we have the biz
intelligence team.

00:28:30.930 --> 00:28:32.100
We have data science.

00:28:32.100 --> 00:28:34.170
We have research team.

00:28:34.170 --> 00:28:37.920
And on top of that, as
well, you have your people

00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:41.310
inside your company, which also
provide a lot of those data.

00:28:41.310 --> 00:28:45.420
So on top of this
complexity, and the variety

00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:50.532
of data that you have,
and that we have,

00:28:50.532 --> 00:28:53.940
we are still experiencing
a growing number--

00:28:53.940 --> 00:28:55.450
volume-- of data.

00:28:55.450 --> 00:28:59.640
So in a month to month
basis, we are growing 32%

00:28:59.640 --> 00:29:00.510
in a month to month.

00:29:00.510 --> 00:29:02.135
And there's our volume
data that we are

00:29:02.135 --> 00:29:04.860
getting from our application.

00:29:04.860 --> 00:29:09.420
And also, we have more than 700
data sources right now that we

00:29:09.420 --> 00:29:11.790
need to aggregate
as a data team,

00:29:11.790 --> 00:29:15.750
and more tens of
thousand of dashboard,

00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:18.810
and all of this combined
with the complexity,

00:29:18.810 --> 00:29:23.400
combined with a very demanding--
but we love them-- user,

00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:26.460
more than 2,000 user
in a weekly app--

00:29:26.460 --> 00:29:28.150
in a weekly basis.

00:29:28.150 --> 00:29:34.650
So everything combined
leads to some major pain

00:29:34.650 --> 00:29:36.880
points that we face
in a daily basis.

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:40.590
And it's not just us, data
team, but also our user, right?

00:29:40.590 --> 00:29:44.370
So first of all, mainly it's--

00:29:44.370 --> 00:29:46.500
it create two main
pain points, which

00:29:46.500 --> 00:29:48.360
is productivity and government.

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:51.270
But in a real sense,
it's actually the times

00:29:51.270 --> 00:29:53.820
that you actually
need to spend when

00:29:53.820 --> 00:29:57.630
you want to search for a
particular question, right?

00:29:57.630 --> 00:30:01.020
You can imagine, like
outside a company, when

00:30:01.020 --> 00:30:04.050
you have a question, you
can simply Google search it,

00:30:04.050 --> 00:30:08.077
and get the reference, read all
through, and provide an answer.

00:30:08.077 --> 00:30:10.410
And you'll want to do the
same when you're in a company,

00:30:10.410 --> 00:30:11.820
right, like us.

00:30:11.820 --> 00:30:13.980
So it just takes too much time.

00:30:13.980 --> 00:30:17.590
A person, for-- to answer
a particular question,

00:30:17.590 --> 00:30:19.693
they would need more
than one hour on average.

00:30:19.693 --> 00:30:21.360
Sometimes, they would
need more than one

00:30:21.360 --> 00:30:24.510
day, because we just
realized that, oops, we

00:30:24.510 --> 00:30:25.750
don't have that data.

00:30:25.750 --> 00:30:28.350
So we might need to
go to the product team

00:30:28.350 --> 00:30:31.710
and actually produce those data.

00:30:31.710 --> 00:30:34.440
And secondly, it's also
taking a lot of time

00:30:34.440 --> 00:30:36.000
for us, product team.

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:38.190
Like, PMs, engineer,
a lot of them

00:30:38.190 --> 00:30:40.500
actually end up going to us.

00:30:40.500 --> 00:30:45.570
Because they want to ask,
hey, I know the data is there.

00:30:45.570 --> 00:30:49.740
But I'm not quite sure whether
the data quality is on track?

00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:53.220
So can you run some query
and check it for us?

00:30:53.220 --> 00:30:55.772
Or, so I know that it is there.

00:30:55.772 --> 00:30:56.730
I checked it by myself.

00:30:56.730 --> 00:30:58.120
The data quality is pretty good.

00:30:58.120 --> 00:31:04.450
But I'm not sure whether it's
already updated for today.

00:31:04.450 --> 00:31:07.920
So a lot of this thing also
adds up to our plate as well.

00:31:07.920 --> 00:31:10.470
And it takes a lot of our
time, which, we are not

00:31:10.470 --> 00:31:11.670
supposed to be doing that.

00:31:11.670 --> 00:31:14.660
We're supposed to be
building products.

00:31:14.660 --> 00:31:17.700
And the last part is,
because people find it hard,

00:31:17.700 --> 00:31:21.870
and it takes too much time
to actually find data,

00:31:21.870 --> 00:31:24.750
they recreate a lot of the
data object that we already

00:31:24.750 --> 00:31:28.530
provide to them, and recreating
a lot of dashboard as well.

00:31:28.530 --> 00:31:32.070
So that's the reason why we
create our own internal tool,

00:31:32.070 --> 00:31:35.490
which is a data discovery tool,
which we call DataDex, which

00:31:35.490 --> 00:31:38.310
basically, it's literally
like a-- we want to build it

00:31:38.310 --> 00:31:41.490
like a Google search for all of
the data that we have at GOJEK.

00:31:41.490 --> 00:31:45.510
So it compiles a lot of
the main data products

00:31:45.510 --> 00:31:49.020
that people are using
inside our company, which

00:31:49.020 --> 00:31:54.150
is BigQuery, the dashboard from
Metabase, and, as well, a lot

00:31:54.150 --> 00:31:57.120
of analyses that are
made from the data teams.

00:31:57.120 --> 00:32:01.560
And what's powerful
with this, it actually

00:32:01.560 --> 00:32:06.910
reduce a lot of the time
that was previously wasted

00:32:06.910 --> 00:32:09.370
to get to the answer quickly.

00:32:09.370 --> 00:32:11.200
So now I'm going to
pass it down to Dimas.

00:32:13.750 --> 00:32:17.320
So Dimas here will talk
about the back end of DataDex

00:32:17.320 --> 00:32:22.160
as well as the limitation,
and why we chose Data Catalog.

00:32:22.160 --> 00:32:23.850
Sorry.

00:32:23.850 --> 00:32:25.500
DIMAS NATAJIWA: OK,
thank you, Renata.

00:32:25.500 --> 00:32:30.570
I believe all of you already
hear how great DataDex is.

00:32:30.570 --> 00:32:33.670
And however, this is
the back end of it.

00:32:33.670 --> 00:32:37.410
So we are using BigQuery as
our main of data sources.

00:32:37.410 --> 00:32:39.670
We have all of the
metadata there.

00:32:39.670 --> 00:32:41.520
And then what happen
is we have one job.

00:32:41.520 --> 00:32:44.080
We're just extracting
all of our metadata.

00:32:44.080 --> 00:32:45.930
And we're grouping
it into its types,

00:32:45.930 --> 00:32:48.990
like which one is the data set,
which one is the tables, which

00:32:48.990 --> 00:32:51.030
one is a column label.

00:32:51.030 --> 00:32:54.210
After that, we store all of
the metadata under the CoSQL

00:32:54.210 --> 00:32:56.670
and export it back to
transform mitigation,

00:32:56.670 --> 00:32:59.280
and push it back to
the elastic search.

00:32:59.280 --> 00:33:01.620
Which, elastic search
will become our back end

00:33:01.620 --> 00:33:04.950
for the DataDex, so it doesn't
need to go to the CoSQL.

00:33:04.950 --> 00:33:07.820
But this needs to go
to the elastic search.

00:33:07.820 --> 00:33:09.660
By having this
architecture, actually, we

00:33:09.660 --> 00:33:11.640
are solving that solution.

00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:13.870
But we create another one.

00:33:13.870 --> 00:33:16.110
So what happened is,
now, our maintenance

00:33:16.110 --> 00:33:17.340
is more and more complex.

00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:20.760
Because once we are giving
BigQuery our metadata,

00:33:20.760 --> 00:33:22.270
a lot of requests
coming in, like,

00:33:22.270 --> 00:33:25.170
can you please provide metadata
for Google Cloud Storage?

00:33:25.170 --> 00:33:28.110
Can you please provide
metadata for Tableau Dashboard?

00:33:28.110 --> 00:33:30.480
All of them are coming
into our requests.

00:33:30.480 --> 00:33:33.720
And the second one
is, our search result

00:33:33.720 --> 00:33:34.870
might be inaccurate.

00:33:34.870 --> 00:33:35.370
Why?

00:33:35.370 --> 00:33:38.190
Because all of these jobs
are running in daily.

00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:40.110
And the third one is
engineering effort

00:33:40.110 --> 00:33:42.780
to maintain all of the
metadata, since the number

00:33:42.780 --> 00:33:47.070
of our BigQuery tables, columns
is increasing instantly.

00:33:47.070 --> 00:33:49.770
Currently, we have more
than 36,000 of table

00:33:49.770 --> 00:33:53.260
and more than 700
column in our BigQuery.

00:33:53.260 --> 00:33:56.390
So when we are facing
this difficulty,

00:33:56.390 --> 00:33:58.530
Data Catalog team came to us.

00:33:58.530 --> 00:34:01.260
And they have Data
Catalog as a solution.

00:34:01.260 --> 00:34:04.050
We are starting
our collaborations

00:34:04.050 --> 00:34:10.300
since July 2, 2018 as an early
access user for this program.

00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:12.570
It's great to have
Shekhar and the team.

00:34:12.570 --> 00:34:15.510
They are really supporting
us for our needs

00:34:15.510 --> 00:34:17.540
in solving that [INAUDIBLE].

00:34:17.540 --> 00:34:23.250
Just an example, they provide
one of the not-GS client API,

00:34:23.250 --> 00:34:25.980
even before it is
released in the alpha.

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:28.949
And beside that, we are also
serving number of development.

00:34:28.949 --> 00:34:30.780
Because we know
there are so many

00:34:30.780 --> 00:34:33.060
feature that will be
available in Data Catalog.

00:34:33.060 --> 00:34:36.310
And we do not need
to developing that.

00:34:36.310 --> 00:34:39.090
So from that profuse
architecture,

00:34:39.090 --> 00:34:42.210
we are going to the
simplicity architecture.

00:34:42.210 --> 00:34:46.469
It's only a DataDex connect
to Data Catalog API.

00:34:46.469 --> 00:34:49.860
What is the advantages by
having this architecture?

00:34:49.860 --> 00:34:52.739
First, there is
really no operation

00:34:52.739 --> 00:34:56.040
required to maintain all of the
infrastructure and availability

00:34:56.040 --> 00:34:57.360
of the metadata.

00:34:57.360 --> 00:34:57.870
Why?

00:34:57.870 --> 00:35:03.300
Because Data Catalog are able
to provide a real-time metadata.

00:35:03.300 --> 00:35:05.690
Once we are creating
a BigQuery table,

00:35:05.690 --> 00:35:09.180
then it will be automatically
showing Data Catalog API.

00:35:09.180 --> 00:35:11.730
And the third one, we
believe, with Data Catalog,

00:35:11.730 --> 00:35:14.250
there will be more and
more feature coming in.

00:35:14.250 --> 00:35:17.910
And it will make us more
focus into creating a business

00:35:17.910 --> 00:35:21.550
and technical metadata
instead of developing the data

00:35:21.550 --> 00:35:24.010
discovery tools.

00:35:24.010 --> 00:35:28.025
OK, I think we can go
through the demo first.

00:35:28.025 --> 00:35:31.390
Let's go to the demo 2.

00:35:31.390 --> 00:35:34.800
RENATA KUMALA: Cool,
OK, let's start.

